<h1>Section 6: Sensing the World</h1>

<div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; font-size: 13px; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Aligns to curriculum Lesson 10</div>

<p>This section prepares you to teach curriculum Lesson 10, where students learn how computers sense the world at all: not with eyes or ears, but with numbers. Students reveal a hidden image hidden inside a grid of bits, then represent a sound as a set of features in a Python dictionary and build a classifier that tells two instruments apart.</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 10:</b> Sensing the World</div>
  <a href="PASTE_UNIT_2_LESSON_10_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 10</a>
</div>

<hr>

<p><b>In this section, you'll:</b></p>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; See how a computer represents an image as a grid of bits, and reveal a hidden image the same way your students will</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Represent a sound as a set of features, frequency, volume, brightness, bundled in a Python dictionary</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; See why two features can both be real and still not be enough to tell two things apart</div>
<div style="font-size: 16px;">&bull; Watch how adding a third feature turns a weak classifier into one that gets 90%+ of notes right</div>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;"><b>&#128161; Notice as you explore:</b> this section is really about representation, not images or sound specifically. The same lesson, a computer only sees what you choose to measure, showed up back in Section 4 and Section 5 as feature selection. Here it shows up again as the difference between a classifier that works and one that doesn't.</div>
</div>

<hr>

<div style="display: flex; gap: 6px; margin-top: 24px; max-width: 700px;">
